WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:04.023
- What's up believe nation.

00:00:04.023 --> 00:00:04.856
It's Evan.

00:00:04.856 --> 00:00:06.819
My one word is believe
and I believe in people

00:00:06.819 --> 00:00:08.500
more than they believe in themselves.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:10.325
I want some of that to rub off onto you,

00:00:10.325 --> 00:00:13.519
so you can go off and
create something fantastic

00:00:13.519 --> 00:00:14.600
and amazing.

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:17.638
Get that thing inside
you out into the world.

00:00:17.638 --> 00:00:19.496
And so to help you on your journey,

00:00:19.496 --> 00:00:21.967
today we're going to look
at the top five books

00:00:21.967 --> 00:00:23.420
or investors.

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:25.982
Coming in at number one is
the Intelligent Investor

00:00:25.982 --> 00:00:27.565
by Benjamin Graham.

00:00:30.694 --> 00:00:33.485
- It's really a pleasure for
me to be able to talk to you

00:00:33.485 --> 00:00:34.557
about Ben Graham.

00:00:34.557 --> 00:00:37.019
I've had some lucky days in my life

00:00:37.019 --> 00:00:41.186
but one of the luckiest was in
1949 when I was 19 years old

00:00:43.567 --> 00:00:45.226
in Lincoln, Nebraska
and I picked up a copy

00:00:45.226 --> 00:00:47.399
of The Intelligent Investor.

00:00:47.399 --> 00:00:50.905
It not only changed my
investment philosophy.

00:00:50.905 --> 00:00:52.448
It really changed my whole life.

00:00:52.448 --> 00:00:55.657
I'd be a different person
or in a different place

00:00:55.657 --> 00:00:59.140
if I hadn't have foreseen that book.

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:02.847
I got a bedrock of investment philosophies

00:01:02.847 --> 00:01:05.464
that really hasn't changed
ever since I read the book.

00:01:05.464 --> 00:01:08.473
I may embellish on it a
little here and there.

00:01:08.473 --> 00:01:12.365
It was Ben's ideas that
sent me down the right path.

00:01:12.365 --> 00:01:14.880
- Coming in at number
two is Rich Dad, Poor Dad

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:16.463
by Robert Kiyosaki.

00:01:19.585 --> 00:01:20.867
- Well you have an anniversary as well,

00:01:20.867 --> 00:01:22.184
your book turns 20 this year

00:01:22.184 --> 00:01:25.184
and has sold over 35 million copies.

00:01:26.859 --> 00:01:29.329
So, do the lessons that
you aim to teach I guess

00:01:29.329 --> 00:01:31.978
20 years ago, 30 years ago rather, 1997,

00:01:31.978 --> 00:01:34.476
do they still resonate today?

00:01:34.476 --> 00:01:36.414
- Oh, they're more important
today than ever before

00:01:36.414 --> 00:01:39.182
because back in the old days 1997

00:01:39.182 --> 00:01:40.722
before you guys were born.

00:01:40.722 --> 00:01:41.699
- [Man] Yeah, I wish.

00:01:41.699 --> 00:01:44.964
- I said your house is not an asset.

00:01:44.964 --> 00:01:46.445
The rich don't work for money

00:01:46.445 --> 00:01:48.483
and savers were losers.

00:01:48.483 --> 00:01:52.781
And in 2000, everything
started to collapse.

00:01:52.781 --> 00:01:55.948
And interest rates dropped below zero,

00:01:57.222 --> 00:01:58.291
which has never happened before.

00:01:58.291 --> 00:02:01.096
People lost their houses, lost their jobs.

00:02:01.096 --> 00:02:03.261
So, it's more important
today than ever before.

00:02:03.261 --> 00:02:06.070
And I'm not really saying
if it's right or wrong,

00:02:06.070 --> 00:02:08.510
I'm just saying we need
financial education.

00:02:08.510 --> 00:02:10.495
What the school teaches about money?

00:02:10.495 --> 00:02:12.191
The answers nothing.

00:02:12.191 --> 00:02:14.199
- Coming in at number three is Flash Boys,

00:02:14.199 --> 00:02:17.366
A Wall Street Revolt by Michael Lewis.

00:02:20.311 --> 00:02:21.935
- This week there is a lot of buzz

00:02:21.935 --> 00:02:24.173
about a provocative new book focusing

00:02:24.173 --> 00:02:27.965
on how it has changed and how
one thousandth of a second

00:02:27.965 --> 00:02:29.436
can make a big difference.

00:02:29.436 --> 00:02:31.775
The book is titled Flash Boys.

00:02:31.775 --> 00:02:35.188
The author is Michael Lewis
who also wrote Money ball,

00:02:35.188 --> 00:02:37.771
Liar's Poker and The Big Short.

00:02:37.771 --> 00:02:39.200
And Michael Lewis joins us now.

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:40.033
Welcome.

00:02:40.033 --> 00:02:40.866
- Thanks for having me.

00:02:40.866 --> 00:02:41.699
